f:["$","p","paragraph-24",{"children":[["$","strong","text-0,bold-0",{"children":"Building Registration"}]," - If your building has more than two units or your landlord (or immediate family) doesn’t live there, your landlord has a duty to register their building. If their registration has lapsed, they can get fined, and may be trying to illegally raise your rent. Report the lack of building registration using our free ",["$","a","hyperlink-2",{"href":"https://app.justfix.org/en/loc/splash?utm_source=who_owns_what","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":[["$","u","text-0,underline-0",{"children":"Letter of Complaint tool"}]]}],", and while you're at it, request your rent history via our ",["$","a","hyperlink-4",{"href":"https://app.justfix.org/en/rh/splash?utm_source=who_owns_what","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":[["$","u","text-0,underline-0",{"children":"Online Form"}]]}]," or by texting “RENT HISTORY” to (646) 783-0627, to check if your apartment is rent stabilized and/or if you’re being overcharged."]}]
10:["$","p","paragraph-25",{"children":[["$","strong","text-0,bold-0",{"children":"“How Is This Building Associated?”"}]," Clicking this link when exploring a portfolio will let you compare the owner names and addresses that two buildings have in common."]}]
11:["$","p","paragraph-26",{"children":[["$","strong","text-0,bold-0",{"children":"Δ Rent Stabilized Units:"}]," Rent stabilized units are apartments that require the landlord to provide a 1 or 2 year lease, and where the rent increase is controlled annually by the Rent Guidelines Board. If the number of rent stabilized units on the right is smaller than the number on the left and appears in red, it means that units have lost their rent stabilized status (have been deregulated), and may mean that the landlord is attempting to push out rent-stabilized tenants."]}]
12:["$","p","paragraph-27",{"children":[["$","strong","text-0,bold-0",{"children":"Open Violations, Total Violations, HPD, and 311: "}]]}]
13:["$","ul","unordered-list-28",{"children":[["$","li","list-item-0",{"children":[["$","p","paragraph-0",{"children":["Building complaints are reported to Housing Preservation and Development (HPD) by calling 311. "]}]]}],["$","li","list-item-1",{"children":[["$","p","paragraph-0",{"children":["Then, HPD sends an inspector to the building to check things out. "]}]]}],["$","li","list-item-2",{"children":[["$","p","paragraph-0",{"children":["Anything the inspector notices is wrong then becomes an “Open Violation” until steps are taken to fix it. "]}]]}],["$","li","list-item-3",{"children":[["$","p","paragraph-0",{"children":["“Total Violations” is a historical count of all Open and Closed Violations. "]}]]}]]}]
